<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $28.83 bln on June 20.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $28.83 bln on June 20.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $28.83 billion on June 20 from $28.58 billion on June 13, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  June 20     June 13	June 21</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     24,876	24,626	17,131</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,954	 3,954	 4,509</p>
<p>    SDRs				     3	     3	   127</p>
<p>    Total			     28,833	28,583	21,767</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
